---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Figure from '../../components/Figure.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/github';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Getting started"
  description="What Semper does, signing in, and image requirements."
  path="/manual/getting-started"
>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 3rem">
    <p class="crumb">
      <a href={withBase('/manual')}>← Manual</a>
    </p>
    <h2>Getting started</h2>
    <p class="sub">What the app returns, how accounts work, and which frames you can load.</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h3>What it does</h3>
      <p>
        You give Semper one <strong>reference</strong> frame (undeformed) and several
        <strong>deformed</strong> frames (one per load step). It matches small windows called
        <strong>subsets</strong> on a grid and returns five maps per frame.
      </p>
      <Figure
        src="/manual/pipeline.svg"
        alt="Pipeline from reference and deformed frames to displacement and strain fields"
        caption="Inputs on the left, matching on the phone, five output fields on the right."
      />
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Field</th>
            <th>Meaning</th>
            <th>Unit</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>U</strong>, <strong>V</strong></td>
            <td>Horizontal / vertical displacement</td>
            <td>px</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Exx</strong>, <strong>Eyy</strong>, <strong>Exy</strong></td>
            <td>Normal and shear strain</td>
            <td>mε (millistrain)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="callout">
        <span class="lead-label">Why it matters:</span> displacements are in
        <strong>pixels</strong> — Semper does not apply a mm scale. Convert with your own factor.
        Correlation runs on the phone; cloud backup only stores results.
      </div>

      <h3>Getting in</h3>
      <p><span class="lead-label">In the app:</span></p>
      <ol>
        <li>Sign in with Google or email.</li>
        <li>
          Email passwords need 8+ characters with upper and lower case, a digit, and a special
          character. Use <strong>Generate secure password</strong> if you want one filled in.
        </li>
        <li>
          After email sign-up, open the verification link, then sign in. Until you verify, sign-in
          is refused.
        </li>
        <li>
          New accounts show <strong>Pending approval</strong>. Support is emailed automatically.
        </li>
        <li>Optional: tap <strong>Request access</strong> to add context in email.</li>
        <li>
          After an admin approves you, tap <strong>Check status</strong>. The screen does not
          refresh by itself.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <Figure
        src="/manual/ui-home.svg"
        alt="Schematic of the Semper Home screen with analysis list and add button"
        caption="Home lists your analyses. Tap to open, long-press to select, + to start a new one."
        phone
      />
      <p>
        <span class="lead-label">If it fails:</span> offline use is fine if this device was approved
        before. Import and solve work without a network; uploads wait until you are online.
      </p>

      <h3>Images it accepts</h3>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Rule</th>
            <th>If it fails</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Every frame matches the reference pixel size</td>
            <td>Blocking error — you cannot run</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>At least one reference and one deformed frame</td>
            <td><strong>Next</strong> stays off</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>At most <em>Max frames</em> (default 50)</td>
            <td>Extras are dropped, with a toast</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        Prefer <strong>PNG</strong> or <strong>TIFF</strong>. JPEG works but Semper warns: compression
        damages the intensity gradients correlation needs. RAW and DNG import only through
        <strong>Files</strong>, not Photos.
      </p>
      <p>
        On import, Semper measures your speckle. A weak pattern shows a low-texture warning and
        suggests a larger subset.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top: 1.5rem">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={withBase('/manual/analysis')}>Open Running an analysis</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={withBase('/manual/faq')}>Open FAQ</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
